## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a scalable, governance-driven data mesh that enables cross-tenant data collaboration while maintaining ownership, privacy, and regulatory controls in Azure.

## Key Concepts

- Data mesh with data products and contracts
- Purview for catalog, lineage, and access governance
- Cross-tenant Data Share and per-tenant RBAC
- Data Lake Gen2 isolation, BYOK, DR, cost governance
- Databricks/Synapse processing, Azure ML private endpoints

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo contract validation for a data product
function validateContract(product) {
  if (!product.contract) throw new Error('Missing contract');
  // check schema, retention, privacy, and access rules
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce data contracts at runtime across tenants?
- What would you monitor for drift and compliance across data products?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical experience designing observable, scalable Azure telemetry pipelines with proper instrumentation, tenant isolation, and comprehensive monitoring integration for enterprise-grade media analytics platforms.

## Key Concepts

- OpenTelemetry integration across Event Hubs, Databricks, and Delta Lake
- End-to-end trace correlation and structured logging
- Adaptive sampling strategies and retention policies
- Tenant-level RBAC and data governance
- Comprehensive monitoring with Application Insights and Azure Monitor
- Real-time alerting and SLA management

## Code Example

```javascript
// Propagate correlation across services
const traceHeader = appInsights.getCorrelationContext();
const traceId = traceHeader.traceId;

// Instrument Event Hubs producer
eventHubProducer.send({
  body: eventData,
  properties: {
    traceId: traceId,
    tenantId: tenantId,
    region: region,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  }
});

// Configure OpenTelemetry sampling
const sampler = new ParentBasedSampler({
  root: new TraceIdRatioBasedSampler(0.01) // 1% production
});
```

